## Implementation and limits

`GenericGuardianWindowsSessionLifecycleCoordinator` uses concrete `GenericGuardianWindowsProcessLifetimeProbe`: only actual Windows PID, fully qualified executable path and OS process creation time can originate or preserve an owner-generated, nonempty Guid epoch for Active/High exact workload identity already resolved in Track3. Repeated identical physical observations preserve exact key object; changed or inaccessible PID/path/start time or invalid state invalidate ownership. `IsCurrent` accepts only the identical issued key object with matching GameId/PID/path and reopens the OS process to verify creation time. Reset invalidates the epoch. The Windows CI tests use the real test runner process; no fake game session is treated as production.

This coordinator is currently STANDALONE. `GenericGuardianWindowsSessionCanaryExecutor` STILL accepts its own caller-supplied `GenericGuardianCanarySessionKey` and does NOT yet call the coordinator at preflight, before mutation or before KEEP; do not present recycled-PID prevention as complete end-to-end. Coordinator does not restore kept mutation leases: future owner host MUST restore all leases before reset/rebind. It cannot attest scene/mode/load/environment or external benchmarks; no production `IGenericGuardianCanaryEvidenceSource`, trusted catalog entries, owner-managed generic host, real-game HIL, auto-activation, physical FPS gain, or causal evidence exists. Track0 generation remains observation, not global exclusion. Preserve BlueStacks/FF specialized host and `main`.

